// `ShapeExtendedType` — the type RTI Connext 7.x ShapesDemo publishes
// when it is started without `-dataType Shape`.
//
// This is NOT a fourth `ShapeType`. It is a different topic type with a
// different name, and SEDP matches it only against other
// `ShapeExtendedType` endpoints. The three files beside it that do
// declare a `ShapeType` are `omg-dds-rtps.idl`, `omg-dds-security.idl`
// and `shapesdemo.idl`; read `README.md` here before you use any of
// them.
//
// Who speaks this one
//   RTI Connext 7.x ShapesDemo in its default mode, and the Fast DDS
//   ShapesDemo build that follows it. On our side
//   `crates/dcps/src/interop.rs` carries a hand-written
//   `ShapeExtendedType`, and the two shapes-demo examples reach it
//   through `ZERODDS_SHAPE_EXTENDED=1`.
//
// Where the declaration comes from
//   Transcribed from the one `crates/dcps/src/interop.rs` quotes in its
//   own doc comment — that is, from what our type claims to be. Whether
//   RTI's shipped `ShapeType.idl` spells it character for character the
//   same is not measured here, and the two suites' files in this
//   directory are the ones that were taken verbatim from a suite
//   checkout. What this file does establish is that the hand-written
//   codec and our IDL front end agree on the octets of the declaration
//   the hand-written codec says it implements.
//
// Why `@final` and why the members are in this order
//   `crates/dcps/src/interop.rs` states both: `@final`, so PLAIN_CDR2
//   under XCDR2 with no DHEADER and the encapsulation id `CDR2_LE`
//   (`0x00 0x07`), XTypes 1.3 Tab. 59; and `fillKind` before `angle`,
//   which is the order RTI's demo writes and therefore the order the
//   octets are in.
//
// Why the enum is not an `octet`
//   XTypes 1.3 §7.3.1.2.1.3 gives an enumeration whose members carry no
//   `@bit_bound` the default bit bound 32, so the discriminant is four
//   octets in the stream's byte order — not one.
//
// What checks it
//   `crates/dcps/tests/shapes_type_idl_agreement.rs` encodes the same
//   values through this file and through the hand-written type and
//   compares the octets, in all four modes the matrix carries.

@extensibility(FINAL)
enum ShapeFillKind {
    SOLID_FILL,
    TRANSPARENT_FILL,
    HORIZONTAL_HATCH,
    VERTICAL_HATCH
};

@extensibility(FINAL)
struct ShapeExtendedType {
    @key string color;
    long x;
    long y;
    long shapesize;
    ShapeFillKind fillKind;
    float angle;
};
